Patch 002: side-by-side identity

What: gives this build its own package id and name so it installs alongside the official app.
In app/build.gradle.kts defaultConfig, adds applicationIdSuffix = ".jf" (package
com.tyraen.voicekeyboard.jf; the FileProvider authority follows via ${applicationId}). In
res/values/strings.xml, sets app_name to "Voice Keyboard (JF)". Namespace, class names and
method.xml are unchanged.

Why: SPEC.md R7 (and N5: the app name carries "(JF)").

When to delete: never, while this fork is installed alongside the official app.

Base: rustemar/voice-keyboard v1.9.1 (02ff1a4bfa626744dfed42b55741f5c55e80060a) with patch 001
applied. Generated with git diff; apply with git apply after 001.

diff --git a/app/build.gradle.kts b/app/build.gradle.kts
index ed6e07d..7c043ef 100644
--- a/app/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/app/build.gradle.kts
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ android {
 
     defaultConfig {
         applicationId = "com.tyraen.voicekeyboard"
+        applicationIdSuffix = ".jf"
         minSdk = 24
         targetSdk = 34
         versionCode = 52
diff --git a/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml b/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
index 837007a..95dddf7 100644
--- a/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
+++ b/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
 <resources>
-    <string name="app_name">Voice Keyboard</string>
+    <string name="app_name">Voice Keyboard (JF)</string>
     <string name="status_idle">Tap mic to record</string>
     <string name="status_recording">Recording\u2026</string>
     <string name="status_transcribing">Transcribing\u2026</string>
